<p>My main research focus is on bridging the gap between symbolic AI and neural networks. Symbolic AI produces knowledge that is directly readable by humans, but is brittle and hard to scale; neural networks are robust and broadly applicable, but the knowledge they encode is hard to access. By combining both approaches, I aim to build AI systems whose knowledge humans can read, check, and build on. My current work ranges from foundation models that induce logical rules from data, to neural networks that learn when to backtrack during reasoning.</p>
